{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "d8d4f869eebc57bcf73fcab65e2bd067e18f578aab0ae6be8fbe2fe4e230a03b", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "6f4914122ede78e3bbee1e4db51c71eacb16e9ec02e12f35cad6310d5abcc28a", "parent_occurrence_id": "d32e3eb7165ff7a08d0bf086e20f7636fd0d4356b9a866a4684f84abb83b3ec1", "source_pointer": "git:4ecb0fe8dda5dc09ef9cb60572440a21c04868af:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:0", "text": "Agent evaluations increasingly depend on context interventions---retrieval, memory graphs, and prompt contracts---yet published reports often omit null outcomes, parser failures, and negative cells."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "7b54d97bd301237be3d759c3a7019af949607ae1ac3d0b38d987fd7ac4411ab4", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "618ad066dcb294ad416da8bba0905ade559af637916d265beef349bb6d2d88a8", "parent_occurrence_id": "d32e3eb7165ff7a08d0bf086e20f7636fd0d4356b9a866a4684f84abb83b3ec1", "source_pointer": "git:4ecb0fe8dda5dc09ef9cb60572440a21c04868af:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:1", "text": "We present HydraDG, a governed experimental framework that binds substantive model invocations, tool calls, and handoffs to \\emph{Fractal Custody Objects} (FCOs) and a \\emph{Fractal Custody Graph} (FCG)."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "340870fe746d637396c8ecb935119d17baa22b94327196f282018b84b9c871b3", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "c8fad34c86bb3b72bf3d56e0ba03e8f5c27333d142c090eed86e511ee3514d54", "parent_occurrence_id": "d32e3eb7165ff7a08d0bf086e20f7636fd0d4356b9a866a4684f84abb83b3ec1", "source_pointer": "git:4ecb0fe8dda5dc09ef9cb60572440a21c04868af:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:2", "text": "HydraDG preregisters hypotheses, freezes case manifests and scorers, records raw prompt and response hashes, and preserves terminal states including timeouts, abstentions, and malformed outputs without silent substitution."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "38260336b22929cd3e6aa7b5f260d60fdd0cc2fbc3fd2429bf4c28f7b571665c", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "a95e5e5b74a2d542e606ce46f3aca53b212cf77fd78b3baf4424f37cec6a8d2d", "parent_occurrence_id": "d32e3eb7165ff7a08d0bf086e20f7636fd0d4356b9a866a4684f84abb83b3ec1", "source_pointer": "git:4ecb0fe8dda5dc09ef9cb60572440a21c04868af:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:3", "text": "We report two preregistered studies (EXP-008, EXP-009) comparing flat prose versus structured FCG retrieval for failure-prevention endpoints; both terminate as \\emph{underpowered} under bounded case replication, so confirmatory effect claims are not supported while negative and null evidence remains in custody."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "5493155d2ebd8441309cae289b6961dc25f56607e972ccfbf4b375a65b4d2bdd", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "1ebd8e54f3b48a1f01ee0afdfe859e65646af91434b5ccbe2b9206c7f8062f33", "parent_occurrence_id": "d32e3eb7165ff7a08d0bf086e20f7636fd0d4356b9a866a4684f84abb83b3ec1", "source_pointer": "git:4ecb0fe8dda5dc09ef9cb60572440a21c04868af:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:4", "text": "We argue that custody-first evaluation infrastructure supports reproducible agent science rather than optional logging."}
